nce&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T09:54:00-07:00","id":1480178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480134-dragon-dragon-flight-examples?p=1480144#post1480144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apep (Egyptian myth) as a Draq maybe. (I don't have a description of the flights beyond their general geographic association available)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Normally I would agree but the manuscript specifically says Apep is a Joka.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T12:16:07-07:00","id":1480193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Storyteller323</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480134-dragon-dragon-flight-examples?p=1480178#post1480178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Normally I would agree but the manuscript specifically says Apep is a Joka.</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason I feel there is a potential adventure arc incorporating the idea that Apep and Tiamat used to date and after a bad breakup they refuse to be in the same Flight and keep disrupting the other's plots just out of spite. This is probably a sign that I watch too much anime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T17:26:26-07:00","id":1480327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480134-dragon-dragon-flight-examples?p=1480193#post1480193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For some reason I feel there is a potential adventure arc incorporating the idea that Apep and Tiamat used to date and after a bad breakup they refuse to be in the same Flight and keep disrupting the other's plots just out of spite. This is probably a sign that I watch too much anime.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At the very least it has the credit of sounding hilarious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T23:18:26-07:00","id":1480451,"title":"","content":"Ironically I think that Quetzalcoatl from &quot;Q the Serpent God&quot; would be some sort of dragonlike monster rather than a true dragon. It expresses no actual intelligence despite it's fairly draconic shape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","name":"Storyteller323","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-08T06:03:21-07:00","id":1480459,"title":"","content":"I suppose the characters from Miss Kobayashi's Dragon Maid would work as more comedic examples of certain types.<br /> <br /> Also Mokole-mbembe as a Jaka perhaps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-08T09:00:03-07:00","id":1480461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1480134-dragon-dragon-flight-examples?p=1480459#post1480459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose the characters from Miss Kobayashi's Dragon Maid would work as more comedic examples of certain types.<br /> <br /> Also Mokole-mbembe as a Jaka perhaps.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If I had to guess, given their predeliction for Chaos, Illulu and Tohru are both probably Draq, Fafnir is a Lindwurm, and given her being constantly hungry Elma <i>might</i> be a Joka? Iirc hunger was a big thing for them. Also ironically though the Loch Ness Monster is a dragon, Mokele-Mbembe is not, the manuscript has them be a three dot birthright creature. I have NO friggin idea for Kanna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12517-storyteller323","user":"Storyteller323","date":". 05-08-2022, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"l